in absentia to the Secretary of the Committee. In case of tie vote, the decision took by the 
Chairperson of the Stipend Support Committee shall prevail. 
51. The meetings of the Stipend Committee shall be documented in minutes, on 
the basis of which the President shall make a decision on awarding stipends to students of 
the University. 
52. Stipend Committee shall be established by the decision of the President of 
the University. President of the University determines the personal membership of the 
Stipend Committee, which includes representatives from: 
1) The Managing Council; 
2) The Academic Council (Schools representatives); 
3) The Faculty Senate; 
4) The Department of Economic Planning and Analysis; 
5) The Department of Student Affairs; 
6) The Bursar’s Office; 
7) The Office of the Registrar; 
8) The Student Government (undergraduate and graduate representatives); 
9) The Legal Department.  
53. The decision of the President also defines the Cha ir, Deputy Chair, and the 
Secretary of the Stipend Committee. 
54. The Chair of the Stipend Committee shall be entitled to:  
1) arrange the work of the Stipend Committee;  
2) convene and chair the meetings of the Stipend Committee;  
3) ensure compliance with the legislation of the Republic of Kazakhstan and the 
University internal regulations when considering issues related to award ing and paying 
stipends. 
55. The Secretary of the Stipend Committee shall:  
1) inform the members about convening of the Stipend Committee;  
2) prepare documents for the meeting, formulate agenda, keep the minutes of 
the meetings;  
3) prepare extracts from the minutes; 
4) perform the recordkeeping of the Stipend Committee documents and transfer 
them in the University storage for keeping in accordance with the established procedures.

